  "decision": "EXTERNAL_IDENTITY_AUTHORITY_WITH_MINIMAL_POSTGRES_SECURITY_SIDECARS",
  "principles": [
    "Firebase/Identity Platform is the authority for identity UID, credential proof, session-cookie validity and global refresh-token revocation.",
    "PostgreSQL is authoritative for canonical platform users, tenant memberships, roles, organization/college status and application authorization.",
    "Never persist raw passwords, Firebase ID/access/refresh tokens, session cookies or raw one-time handoff codes.",
    "A PostgreSQL sidecar is allowed only when it preserves a concrete product/audit/concurrency job not represented by the provider, and it must fail closed with keyed digests/MACs.",
    "Provider acceptance and PostgreSQL migration replay remain separate DONE_VERIFIED gates."
  ],
